  "description": "Returned by garminconnect's get_respiration_data(date). Consumed by sync_respiration.\n\nVerified against: 2026-07-28, 2026-07-15, 2026-08-05. Additional fields beyond what's listed here may exist and are tolerated (additionalProperties: true) \u2014 Garmin adding new fields is not a breaking change; a listed field disappearing or changing type is.\n\n2026-08-05 (via automatic drift-check on live data, #68): avgTomorrowSleepRespirationValue and the four tomorrowSleep*Timestamp* fields observed null (no next-day sleep prediction yet available) \u2014 now nullable rather than required-present. respirationAveragesValuesArray's inner values observed as floats (e.g. 14.11), not integers, and null-padded in the day's last row \u2014 widened to integer|number|null. None of these fields are consumed by sync_respiration (only lowest/highest/avgWaking/avgSleepRespirationValue are), so this was schema over-strictness, not a real API change."
